   exact residue of G at the n-th pole: e^{sigma m^2}/(2 i E_n): on shell P^2=-m^2, so the
   O(d)-covariant Gaussian kernel does NOT suppress the alias states at all.
   => one field per site, but a pole (one-particle state) for every n_1: the complete
      reciprocal-lattice tower; the remnant translation acts on the n-th state as i(k_1+2 pi n_1)
      and the time component as -E_n (energy): continuum momentum on the folded continuum.
